# Day 6 — Data Preprocessing & Feature Engineering 🔧

80% of a data scientist's work is cleaning and preparing data. Even the best machine learning algorithm performs badly on messy data. Clean data + simple algorithm usually beats dirty data + advanced algorithm.

Real-world data always contains problems such as:
- Missing values
- Wrong formatting
- Outliers
- Incorrect data types
- Inconsistent categories

Example:

| Name   | Age | City       | Salary | Joined |
|--------|-----|------------|--------|---------|
| Rahul  | 25  | Hyderabad  | 50000  | 2021-03-15 |
| Priya  | NaN | mumbai     | 999999 | 2019-07-22 |
| Kiran  | 19  | BANGALORE  | 45000  | NaN |
| Ananya | 200 | Chennai    | 62000  | 2020-11-08 |
| Ravi   | 28  | hyderabad  | 58000  | 2022-01-30 |

Problems:
- Missing values (NaN)
- Inconsistent text formatting
- Outliers like age=200
- Wrong salary values
- Missing dates

Data preprocessing means fixing all these problems before training the model.

--------------------------------------------------

# 🔥 Handling Missing Values

Missing values are one of the most common problems in datasets.

Different strategies are used based on the situation.

--------------------------------------------------

# ✅ Missing Value Handling Code

```python
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np

data = {
    'Name': ['Rahul', 'Priya', 'Kiran', 'Ananya', 'Ravi', 'Sara', 'Amit'],
    'Age': [25, np.nan, 19, 45, np.nan, 32, 28],
    'City': ['Hyderabad', 'Mumbai', np.nan, 'Chennai', 'Hyderabad', np.nan, 'Mumbai'],
    'Salary': [50000, 80000, 45000, np.nan, 58000, 72000, np.nan],
    'Score': [85, 90, np.nan, 78, 88, np.nan, 92]
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)

# Check missing values
print(df.isnull().sum())

# Percentage of missing values
print(df.isnull().mean() * 100)

# Mean fill
df['Age'] = df['Age'].fillna(df['Age'].mean())

# Median fill
df['Salary'] = df['Salary'].fillna(df['Salary'].median())

# Mode fill
df['City'] = df['City'].fillna(df['City'].mode()[0])

# Forward fill
df['Score'] = df['Score'].fillna(method='ffill')

print(df)
````

---

# 📌 When to Use Which Method

| Method       | Use Case                        |
| ------------ | ------------------------------- |
| Mean Fill    | Numerical data without outliers |
| Median Fill  | Numerical data with outliers    |
| Mode Fill    | Categorical columns             |
| Forward Fill | Time series data                |
| Drop Rows    | Very few missing rows           |
| Drop Column  | More than 50% values missing    |

