# 🔥 Feature Scaling

Feature scaling brings all features into similar range.

Example:

* Salary → 50000
* Age → 25

Without scaling, larger values dominate the model.

Two popular scaling methods:

* StandardScaler
* MinMaxScaler

---

# ✅ StandardScaler vs MinMaxScaler

```python
from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, MinMaxScaler
import numpy as np

data = np.array([[1000], [2000], [3000], [4000], [5000]])

# StandardScaler
ss = StandardScaler()

print(ss.fit_transform(data))

# MinMaxScaler
mms = MinMaxScaler()

print(mms.fit_transform(data))
```

---

# 📌 Difference Between Both

| Scaler         | Description                 |
| -------------- | --------------------------- |
| StandardScaler | Mean=0 and Std=1            |
| MinMaxScaler   | Scales data between 0 and 1 |

---

# 📌 When to Use Which

| Method         | Best Use                             |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| StandardScaler | Regression, Logistic Regression, SVM |
| MinMaxScaler   | Neural Networks                      |

