# 🔥 Outlier Detection and Removal

Outliers are extreme values that do not follow normal pattern.

Example:

Ages:
[22, 25, 28, 24, 26, 200, 23]

Here 200 is an outlier.

Outliers can badly affect machine learning models.

---

# ✅ IQR Method

Most commonly used outlier detection method.

```python
import pandas as pd

data = {
    'Salary': [
        30000,
        35000,
        40000,
        42000,
        38000,
        36000,
        500000,
        39000
    ]
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)

Q1 = df['Salary'].quantile(0.25)

Q3 = df['Salary'].quantile(0.75)

IQR = Q3 - Q1

lower = Q1 - 1.5 * IQR

upper = Q3 + 1.5 * IQR

print("Lower:", lower)
print("Upper:", upper)

outliers = df[
    (df['Salary'] < lower) |
    (df['Salary'] > upper)
]

print(outliers)

# Remove outliers
df_clean = df[
    (df['Salary'] >= lower) &
    (df['Salary'] <= upper)
]

print(df_clean)
```

---

# ✅ Z-Score Method

```python
from scipy import stats
import numpy as np

salaries = [
    30000,
    35000,
    40000,
    42000,
    38000,
    36000,
    500000
]

z_scores = np.abs(stats.zscore(salaries))

print(z_scores)

outlier_indices = np.where(z_scores > 3)[0]

print(outlier_indices)
```

---

# 📌 IQR vs Z-Score

| Method  | Description                 |
| ------- | --------------------------- |
| IQR     | Works on any distribution   |
| Z-Score | Assumes normal distribution |

